#compdef pmap

# Parallel map: `pmap 'cmd {}' ITEM...` runs the template once per ITEM
# on the worker pool, `{}` replaced by the item, output printed in input
# order.
#
# zshrs builtin. This file shadows the stock zsh `_pmap`, which completes
# the Solaris/procps process-memory-map command; the zshrs builtin of the
# same name is unrelated to it.
#
# Arguments mirror builtin_pmap (src/extensions/ext_builtins.rs): argv[0]
# is the template, argv[1..] the items, no options; keep in sync.
# Bundled into ~/.zshrs/functions by build.rs.

_arguments \
    '1:command template ({} is replaced by each item):_cmdstring' \
    '*:item:_files'
